{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WetDepLS",
    "description": "WRF-Chem's large-scale (grid-scale) wet deposition of ONE species over one column, `wetdep_ls` in chem/module_wetdep_ls.F (WRF v4.8.0), the scheme `wetscav_onoff < 0` selects. It is the only wet-scavenging path reachable with this project's chem_opt = 170 physics suite (WSM6 + New Tiedtke): `wetscav_onoff = 1` is fatal for chem_opt 170 and for mp_physics 6 in chemics_init, and convective-transport scavenging (`chem_conv_tr`, `conv_tr_wetscav`) needs a Grell-family cumulus scheme (FORTRAN_BUGS.md N115; that path also carries two defects of its own, B23 and B24). The species loop is a mapping, not physics -- the scheme treats every species alike apart from its efficiency `alpha` and the burden gate -- so the consumer maps this component over the species it scavenges: every aerosol species of the mechanism (nv > numgas: MOSAIC's mass, number AND water of all eight bins, at alpha = 0.5) and gas-phase sulfuric acid (`sulf`, alpha = 1). Every other gas is untouched.\n\nThe scheme. With R = rain/dt the step's grid-scale rain rate (WRF's `rainncv`, mm per step), it forms the column-integrated upward cloud-water flux C = integral of max(0, qc rho w) dz, and a conversion factor frc = clamp(R/C, 1e-6, 0.005), the fraction of that flux that falls as rain. Each layer then loses alpha f/(1+f) of the species, with f = frc rho dz w, the scavenged value floored at 1e-16. The tendency a consumer integrating the column must add is the operator-split increment over the step, `dc_dt = (c_out - c)/dt` (CLAUDE.md, operator-split schemes): the Fortran is an in-place update with no rate inside it, and its removal fraction f/(1+f) is the implicit-Euler form of a first-order loss at rate f/dt, so the increment converges to that loss as the step shrinks.\n\nWhat the scheme does that its comments do not say, all reproduced here. (1) The removal argument f is DIMENSIONALLY INCONSISTENT: frc carries 1/m, so f is a mass flux in kg m-2 s-1 that the Fortran adds to 1; the component divides by a unit flux `F_unit` to reproduce WRF's number (FORTRAN_BUGS.md B22). (2) `w` is WRF's `w_2(i,k,j)`, the vertical velocity on the BOTTOM face of layer k, not the layer's own; the surface face has w = 0, so the lowest layer is never scavenged. (3) The column sum runs over layers 1..NLEV-1 and the removal over 1..NLEV-2 (`k=1,kte-1` and `k=kts,kte-2` with kte = NLEV), so the top layer is excluded from the integral and the top two from the removal. (4) The burden gate is a plain level sum of c rho with no layer thickness, compared with a bare 1e-10 in whatever unit the species is carried in. (5) The removal needs qc > 0 in the layer but is not proportional to it: a layer with a trace of cloud water and a large updraught loses as much as a saturated one.\n\nInputs are consumer-supplied column fields (parameters with shape `lev`), following the column convention: real geometry `ze` from the consumer, the layer count a metaparameter.\n\nWhat the tests pin and what they cannot. Twelve tests, one model step and one species each, from a capture that switches the scheme on (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_wetscav.sh: the reference column with wetscav_onoff = -1 and cu_physics = 0, steps 1300-1480 spanning a dry step, the onset at 2.7e-9 mm of rain, the 0.45 mm/step peak and the tail). Each asserts the activation flag exactly and the scavenged column and its tendency at 1e-9 of the column maximum against the real64 replay of the dumped inputs through chem/module_wetdep_ls.F compiled unchanged; the in-model real32 result agrees with that replay to 5.7e-8 of the column maximum over all 101 dumped steps and all 233 species. Mutation checks: dropping the qc > 0 layer gate fails 22 assertions, scavenging sulf at the aerosol efficiency fails 6, and moving the frc clamp from 0.005 to 0.01 fails 2. Quirk (3) is NOT exercised: extending the removal to layer NLEV-1 or the integral to layer NLEV fails nothing, because the top layers of this 20 km column never carry cloud water. The intermediates (cw_column, frc, f) are not taped by the kernel and are unasserted; they are pinned through the outputs they feed.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-11T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "wet-deposition",
      "wetdep_ls",
      "chem_opt-170",
      "column"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "WRF-Chem v4.8.0, chem/module_wetdep_ls.F (subroutine wetdep_ls), called from chem/chem_driver.F when wetscav_onoff < 0."
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Mass layers of the column, WRF kte (= e_vert - 1). Bound into the column grid at the import edge."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "WetDepLS": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_whole.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "par": {
          "ref": "./wetdep_ls_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "c": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The species, in its WRF chem unit (ppmv for sulf; ug/kg for an aerosol mass, 1/kg for a number). The scheme's gates compare it with bare numbers in that unit, so it is declared dimensionless here and the gates carry the unit of the comparison."
        },
        "qc": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Cloud-water mixing ratio, moist(:,:,:,p_qc)."
        },
        "rho": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "default": 1.0,
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Air density as chem_driver passes it, `rho`."
        },
        "w": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Vertical velocity on the BOTTOM face of each layer, WRF `w_2(i,k,j)` as chem_driver copies it into `vvel` (k = 1 is the surface face, w = 0)."
        },
        "ze": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Heights of the layer faces; only their differences, the layer thicknesses (WRF dz8w), enter."
        },
        "rain": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^2",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Grid-scale rain over the step, WRF `rainncv` (mm per step, i.e. kg m-2)."
        },
        "dt": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 60.0,
          "description": "The model step the rain was accumulated over, `grid%dt`."
        },
        "alpha": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.5,
          "description": "Scavenging efficiency of this species: par.alpha_aerosol for an aerosol species, par.alpha_sulf for sulf."
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer thickness, WRF dz8w, from the grid template."
        },
        "z_sfc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Bottom of the column, the integral's lower bound."
        },
        "z_top": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Top of the column, the integral's upper bound."
        },
        "rain_rate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/(m^2*s)",
          "description": "Grid-scale rain rate, `rain_clw = rain/dt`."
        },
        "cw_flux": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/(m^2*s)",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Upward cloud-water flux density of each layer, max(0, qc rho w), on the layers the column integral covers (1..NLEV-1) and zero on the top layer."
        },
        "cw_column": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/(m*s)",
          "description": "Column-integrated upward cloud-water flux, `var_sum_clw`."
        },
        "burden": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "description": "Level sum of c rho over layers 1..NLEV-1, `var_sum` (no layer thickness: a gate, not a burden in the physical sense)."
        },
        "active": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when the column scavenges this species at all -- rain, burden and cloud-water flux each above their gate -- else 0."
        },
        "frc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/m",
          "description": "Conversion factor, rain rate over cloud-water flux clamped into [frc_min, frc_max]; 0 when inactive."
        },
        "f": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Per-layer removal argument max(0, frc rho dz w), divided by par.F_unit (see the model description)."
        },
        "removal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Fraction of the species the layer loses this step, alpha f/(1+f) where the layer is scavenged (active column, layer 1..NLEV-2, c above threshold, qc > 0), else 0."
        },
        "c_out": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The species after the step's wet deposition, floored at par.c_threshold where scavenged."
        },
        "dc_dt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The operator-split tendency (c_out - c)/dt a consumer integrating the column adds."
        }
      },
